# Vault sync (Obsidian)

This project uses `Vault/` as durable context for AI tools (Obsidian). Cursor agents must keep the vault aligned with meaningful code changes.

## Before coding

- Read `Vault/Features/<Feature Name>.md` when it exists and the task is feature work.
- If no feature note exists and the task is more than a trivial one-line fix, create one from `Vault/Templates/Feature Brief.md` in `Vault/Features/`.

## After coding (before finishing)

Update the vault when work is **meaningful** (feature slice, behavior change, decision, or gotcha):

1. **Feature note** (`Vault/Features/<name>.md`):
   - **Shipped** — date, summary, key files, tests run
   - **Gotchas** — non-obvious behavior, auth/financial risks, things the next agent must know
   - Check off completed **Acceptance criteria**
   - Update **Open questions** if any remain
2. **Decision** — if architecture/product choice was made, add or update a note from `Vault/Templates/Decision Record.md` or link from `Vault/Domains/`.
3. **Global invariants** — if wallet, auth, routing, or stack rules changed, update `SYSTEM_CONTEXT_CORE_v1.md` §0 or §16 only (not the whole file).

## Mid-session handoff

If work stops before shipping, use `Vault/Templates/Session Handoff.md` instead of filling **Shipped**.

## Vault writing rules

- Bullets, plain language, no full code dumps.
- Minimal edits — append/update sections; do not rewrite entire notes.
- Do not create markdown outside `Vault/` unless Omar explicitly asks (except `SYSTEM_CONTEXT_CORE_v1.md` for global invariants).

## When to skip

Skip vault edits for trivial changes (typo, formatting, rename with no behavior change). Say so explicitly.

## Required reply footer

End every Agent response with:

```text
Vault sync: <files updated> | skipped (trivial) | handoff only
```
